From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Charlie <5764343+charlielye@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 10:57:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(kv-store): run the browser store on
 @aztec-labs/kv-sqlite, and the same store anywhere

kv-store's containers (map, multimap, array, set, singleton) call the Kv service's generated
client instead of writing SQL, in AztecKvSqliteStore (@aztec-labs/kv-store/kv-sqlite), which
takes any of the service's backends: its native library or process in node, the library through
JSI in React Native, the wasm module in a browser.

AztecSQLiteOPFSStore keeps its API, Web Lock and quarantine. Its worker runs the service's wasm
module on its own thread with an OPFS `files` target (opfs_files.ts) that keeps the opfs-sahpool
layout, so stores written so far open unchanged, encrypted ones included; the main thread posts
the client's command bytes to it. sqlite3mc-wasm remains only for the cut-commit test, which
writes a store through its own pool VFS.

